            "review_title": "Review at Lua Café Old Saigon Art Exhibition",
            "review_text": "Kyle Ng\nWorld6 contributions\n1\nA Vietnamese version of \"American Pickers\" series.\nSep 2023 • Family\nThis place is amazing. A grand exhibition of Southern Vietnam combined with a cafe restaurant serving authentic dishes and drinks such as \"banh canh\", \"bo ne\", and traditional drip coffee. It took me back to my childhood in Saigon that I thought I had lost long ago. Very natural and traditional, friendly, much better than going to museums. And you can stay here all day without paying an entrance fee. Of course, paying for a cup of coffee or a meal is the right thing to do.\n\nI wish the owner of this place did better marketing. This is a must-visit place for tourists to understand the life and people of Southern Vietnam, but not many tourists know about this place because they don't do marketing or advertisement and only rely on word of mouth.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten September 22, 2023",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-05",
