            "review_title": "Review at Lua Café Old Saigon Art Exhibition",
            "review_text": "Alice A\n8 contributions\n1\nA hidden gem of Saigon, must-see place if you want to truly appreciate the life and culture of Southern Vietnam\nSep 2023 • Friends\nLua Café Old Saigon Art Exhibition is a hidden gem of Saigon. It is located on the avenue that connects the international airport and the city center, only 10 minutes away from the airport and 15 minutes by car from the city center. It offers a unique opportunity to experience and understand the lives of the people of South Vietnam in the past. The exterior may look plain as a normal café, but the interior is beautiful, warm and welcoming, with a collection of old Saigon artifacts as impressive as a private museum. No wonder this place holds the Vietnam record for displaying antiques of Southern Vietnam.\n\nMy only regret is that I didn't have enough time to explore the place. It surpassed my expectations of a \"personal museum\" in the heart of a nostalgic cafe.\n\nThis hidden gem will take your breath away and I highly recommend it as a must-see place in Saigon if you want to truly appreciate the life and culture of Southern Vietnam.\nRead more\nWritten September 20, 2023",
